### 1.3 The Primordial Waters (*Omi Ipilẹ*) as Cosmic Substrate

In Yoruba creation cosmology, the original state of the cosmos prior to the manifest world (*Ilẹ*) was *Omi Ipilẹ*—the primordial, boundless, and unformed waters governed by *Olokun*. Solid land and physical form were not created by destroying or replacing these waters; rather, land was sculpted *upon* and *within* them.

This cosmological architecture directly models what theoretical physics terms the quantum vacuum or the zero-point field—a continuum of boundless, unmanifested potentiality. Because the primordial fluid state remains the underlying substrate of all physical reality, any interaction within the physical realm is an interaction *through* water.

Within this framework, consciousness (*Eniyan*) and physical reality (*Ayé*) do not interact as two foreign substances meeting across an empty void. They are two currents flowing within the same primordial medium (*Omi Ipilẹ*). This fluid ontology provides the necessary theoretical bridge for the **AEVOV Quantum Mirror Theory**, replacing the paradigm of wave function collapse with a model of fluid resonance, reflection, and non-local entanglement.

